{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The problem does not contain a sure outcome (i.e., no 100% probability outcome), so the reference value is zero. The reason evaluates each outcome by its difference from this reference (which, since the reference is zero, equals the outcome itself) and weights these differences by their probabilities to compute a mean difference. For Lottery A: (4000 - 0)*0.25 + (2000 - 0)*0.25 + (0 - 0)*0.50 = 1000 + 500 + 0 = 1500. For Lottery B: (6000 - 0)*0.25 + (0 - 0)*0.75 = 1500. The mean differences are equal (1500 for both), so the reason would be indifferent between A and B.",
